        {
          "name": "SetApiKeyPolicy",
          "path": "auth.v1.PolicyService/SetApiKeyPolicy",
          "requestType": "auth.v1.SetApiKeyPolicyRequest",
          "responseType": "auth.v1.SetApiKeyPolicyResponse",
          "summary": "Set API Key Policy",
          "doc": "Attach a policy to a key, apply a template to it as a new copy, or clear\n its policy. Attaching a policy that allows a money-out action to an\n assistant API key returns FailedPrecondition with\n AUTH_ASSISTANT_KEY_ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED, and applying a template to one\n returns FailedPrecondition with AUTH_POLICY_INVALID.\n\n An admin API key with MANAGE_API_KEY_POLICIES may also attach, apply or\n clear the policy of a standard key it may manage, without a session; the\n key needs an IP allowlist within the admin key's own. The policy can never\n allow a money-out action (AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_FORBIDDEN_TARGET) or an admin\n permission (AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_ESCALATION_DENIED), and on a sub-account key\n never more actions or markets than the sub-account's policy\n (AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_SCOPE_EXCEEDED), each PermissionDenied. Attaching a\n money-out policy to an admin key returns FailedPrecondition with\n AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED.",
          "tags": [
            "account"
          ],
          "authRequired": true,
          "authenticationMethods": [
            "session_token",
            "api_key"
          ],
          "mfaRequirement": "conditional",
          "stability": "stable",
          "errorProtoPkg": "auth.v1",
          "errorCatalog": "core:generic",
          "examples": {
            "request": {
              "keyId": "ak_1a3c6de8153d5a5b04cd2a6529779542",
              "policyId": "2779655768052592500"
            },
            "response": {
              "policyId": "2779655768052592500"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "SetSubaccountPolicy",
          "path": "auth.v1.PolicyService/SetSubaccountPolicy",
          "requestType": "auth.v1.SetSubaccountPolicyRequest",
          "responseType": "auth.v1.SetSubaccountPolicyResponse",
          "summary": "Set Subaccount Policy",
          "doc": "Attach a policy to a sub-account, apply a template to it as a new copy, or\n clear its policy.\n\n An admin API key with MANAGE_SUBACCOUNT_POLICIES may also attach, apply or\n clear the policy of a sub-account the main account owns, without a\n session. It can never attach or apply a policy that allows a money-out\n action, replace a locked policy, or reach a sub-account shared with the\n main account: PermissionDenied with AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_FORBIDDEN_TARGET.\n\n A sub-account a strategy bot holds or held keeps the bot's trading-only\n policy: attaching or applying another is FailedPrecondition with\n AUTH_STRATEGY_BOT_MANAGED. Once the bot's access has ended, its policy\n can be cleared.",
          "tags": [
            "account"
          ],
          "authRequired": true,
          "authenticationMethods": [
            "session_token",
            "api_key"
          ],
          "mfaRequirement": "conditional",
          "stability": "stable",
          "errorProtoPkg": "auth.v1",
          "errorCatalog": "core:generic",
          "examples": {
            "request": {
              "policyId": "2779655768052592500",
              "subaccountId": "6789012345678"
            },
            "response": {
              "policyId": "2779655768052592500"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "UpdateApiPolicy",
          "path": "auth.v1.PolicyService/UpdateApiPolicy",
          "requestType": "auth.v1.UpdateApiPolicyRequest",
          "responseType": "auth.v1.UpdateApiPolicyResponse",
          "summary": "Update API Key Policy",
          "doc": "Change selected fields on an existing API key policy. Editing a template\n changes only the template: keys it was applied to keep their copies.\n Adding a money-out action to a policy attached to an assistant API key\n returns FailedPrecondition with AUTH_ASSISTANT_KEY_ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED, and\n to a policy attached to an admin API key FailedPrecondition with\n AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED.",
          "tags": [
            "account"
          ],
          "authRequired": true,
          "authenticationMethods": [
            "session_token"
          ],
          "mfaRequirement": "fresh_step_up",
          "stability": "stable",
          "errorProtoPkg": "auth.v1",
          "errorCatalog": "core:generic",
          "examples": {
            "request": {
              "expectedRevision": "1",
              "policy": {
                "name": "value"
              },
              "policyId": "2779655768052592500",
              "updateMask": "name"
            },
            "response": {
              "policy": {
                "actions": [
                  "TRADE_SPOT"
                ],
                "createdAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                "description": "Allow market and account data reads.",
                "id": "2462848330134654640",
                "isTemplate": false,
                "name": "Read-Only Analytics",
                "revision": "1",
                "sourceTemplateId": "4015734498775142139",
                "sourceTemplateRevision": "1",
                "spotMarketScope": "ALL",
                "spotMarkets": [
                  {
                    "symbolId": 1
                  }
                ],
                "updatedAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "UpdateSubaccountPolicy",
          "path": "auth.v1.PolicyService/UpdateSubaccountPolicy",
          "requestType": "auth.v1.UpdateSubaccountPolicyRequest",
          "responseType": "auth.v1.UpdateSubaccountPolicyResponse",
          "summary": "Update Subaccount Policy",
          "doc": "Change selected fields on an existing sub-account policy. Editing a\n template changes only the template: sub-accounts it was applied to keep\n their copies.\n\n An admin API key with MANAGE_SUBACCOUNT_POLICIES may also update a policy\n of the main account's own sub-accounts without a session. The result can\n never allow a money-out action, and it can never lock, unlock or change a\n locked policy: PermissionDenied with AUTH_ADMIN_KEY_FORBIDDEN_TARGET.\n\n A sub-account a strategy bot holds or held keeps the bot's trading-only\n policy: FailedPrecondition with AUTH_STRATEGY_BOT_MANAGED.",
          "tags": [
            "account"
          ],
          "authRequired": true,
          "authenticationMethods": [
            "session_token",
            "api_key"
          ],
          "mfaRequirement": "conditional",
          "stability": "stable",
          "errorProtoPkg": "auth.v1",
          "errorCatalog": "core:generic",
          "examples": {
            "request": {
              "expectedRevision": "1",
              "policy": {
                "name": "value"
              },
              "policyId": "2779655768052592500",
              "updateMask": "name"
            },
            "response": {
              "policy": {
                "actions": [
                  "TRADE_SPOT"
                ],
                "createdAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                "description": "Allow spot trading for selected markets.",
                "expiresAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                "id": "2462848330134654640",
                "isTemplate": false,
                "locked": false,
                "maxOpenOrders": 1,
                "maxOrderNotional": "12345",
                "name": "Market Maker Policy",
                "reviewAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                "revision": "1",
                "sourceTemplateId": "4015734498775142139",
                "sourceTemplateRevision": "1",
                "spotMarketScope": "ALL",
                "spotMarkets": [
                  {
                    "symbolId": 1
                  }
                ],
                "tradingHalted": false,
                "updatedAt": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z"
              }
            }
          }
